      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GV9Hpa1yEPPZWmJ-_M2A3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5245.876901994879,
      "y": 852.0936756937185,
      "width": 1397.4408644377722,
      "height": 240.52661886056293,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cMsq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 681595692,
      "version": 556,
      "versionNonce": 664129182,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788587777156,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Misassumption about monolith design & microservice arch:\n- whole code runs on single machine in monolith (we cannot scale individual \n  module or service but we can scale whole app\n- ppl assume that all services runs on different machines. ( we can run but\n  it done mostly when need scaling )",
      "fontSize": 38.48425901769007,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Misassumption about monolith design & microservice arch:\n- whole code runs on single machine in monolith (we cannot scale individual \n  module or service but we can scale whole app\n- ppl assume that all services runs on different machines. ( we can run but\n  it done mostly when need scaling )",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SKbOvKPlxTa1elHLVekZQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5242.259274383971,
      "y": 1112.9800643638027,
      "width": 1628.2313227985594,
      "height": 240.52661886056293,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cMsr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2141547948,
      "version": 437,
      "versionNonce": 543846978,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788587777156,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "From monolith to microservice convert:\n- Not one day Activity\n- pure k pure system ko ek saaath migrate nhi karte ( ek ek karke karenge as needed )\n- after conversion of a specific service to microservice we cannot transport 100% \n  traffic to that microervice",
      "fontSize": 38.48425901769007,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "From monolith to microservice convert:\n- Not one day Activity\n- pure k pure system ko ek saaath migrate nhi karte ( ek ek karke karenge as needed )\n- after conversion of a specific service to microservice we cannot transport 100% \n  traffic to that microervice",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MYDeEubgt_w-aI3Y4jS1y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5243.272189739649,
      "y": 1380.7763974323018,
      "width": 1776.8958775821875,
      "height": 1779.8969795681658,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cMss",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1477280020,
      "version": 1867,
      "versionNonce": 1197361886,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788587777156,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Amazon example:\n- Understand your monolith\n- Identify high impact areas (point 2 in from monolith to microservice convert)\n- build API contracts and\n  setup communication (two types 1.sync(REST, gRPC etc.) 2.async(kafka rabbitmq etc)\n- module by module migration ( slowly slowly ek ek module ko microservice banao )\n- Monitoring and observability\n- scaling and optimization\n- do not stop or terminate a service or module in monolith until 100% traffic shift to \n  that respective microservice.\n  = traffic ko kese shift or handle karenge\n    i) traffic ( Canary deployment ) - small subset od users ko shift kar dete hai microservice \n      pe pehle then check ki utne user k liye thik kaam karta hai then increase shifting of \n      user then then check and continues (eg, check for 0.1% then 1% then 5% and continue...)\n    ii) Strangler design pattern (a microservice design pattern)\n    iii) Manage Transaction ( SAGA Design patterns )\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    iv) Data consistency Management (OutBox pattern)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- After compleitng whole these steps code transfer and user transfer\n  100% the monolith is transfered to microservice",
      "fontSize": 38.48425901769007,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Amazon example:\n- Understand your monolith\n- Identify high impact areas (point 2 in from monolith to microservice convert)\n- build API contracts and\n  setup communication (two types 1.sync(REST, gRPC etc.) 2.async(kafka rabbitmq etc)\n- module by module migration ( slowly slowly ek ek module ko microservice banao )\n- Monitoring and observability\n- scaling and optimization\n- do not stop or terminate a service or module in monolith until 100% traffic shift to \n  that respective microservice.\n  = traffic ko kese shift or handle karenge\n    i) traffic ( Canary deployment ) - small subset od users ko shift kar dete hai microservice \n      pe pehle then check ki utne user k liye thik kaam karta hai then increase shifting of \n      user then then check and continues (eg, check for 0.1% then 1% then 5% and continue...)\n    ii) Strangler design pattern (a microservice design pattern)\n    iii) Manage Transaction ( SAGA Design patterns )\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    iv) Data consistency Management (OutBox pattern)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- After compleitng whole these steps code transfer and user transfer\n  100% the monolith is transfered to microservice",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
