    {
      "id": "DD2j9tDpPMT05Ax9_q5DJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 31277.984152970243,
      "y": 1864.6894090455685,
      "width": 979.4391479492188,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cNZ6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1672868926,
      "version": 537,
      "versionNonce": 735308994,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788587777185,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3.indes and cache inefficiency\n--> Indexes speeed up queries - but\n1. when tables grow huge, indexes themselves become large and heavy\n2. Updating data means updating indexes too -> more work per write.\n3. As cache (like DB buffer cache) fills up, lessfrequently used data gets evicted, forcing disk reads\n\nResult: Queries that once hit memory now hit disk, slowing things down drastically.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3.indes and cache inefficiency\n--> Indexes speeed up queries - but\n1. when tables grow huge, indexes themselves become large and heavy\n2. Updating data means updating indexes too -> more work per write.\n3. As cache (like DB buffer cache) fills up, lessfrequently used data gets evicted, forcing disk reads\n\nResult: Queries that once hit memory now hit disk, slowing things down drastically.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
